--TEST--
a `lateinit` property on a `#[Json\Derive]` class and a `secret` one on a `#[Db\Derive]` class are refused at the declaration, and a call that encodes a class whose `secret` property the decoder fills does not compile — `rule:core-classes/derive-property-list`, `rule:security/derived-codec-qualifiers`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:attributes/core-json-derive-and-core-json-field-a-class-with-a-json-codec
class Session {
    public string $id;
    public function constructor(string $id) {
        $this->id = $id;
    }
}

#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Account {
    public secret string $apiKey;
    lateinit public Session $session;

    public function constructor(secret string $apiKey) {
        $this->apiKey = $apiKey;
    }
}

#[Core\Db\Derive]
class Key {
    public secret string $token;
    public function constructor(secret string $token) {
        $this->token = $token;
    }
}

#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Team {
    public ?Account $owner;
    public function constructor(?Account $owner) {
        $this->owner = $owner;
    }
}

array<Team> $teams = [];
echo Core\Json::encode($teams);
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0463]: `$session` is `lateinit`, so `#[Json\Derive]` cannot convert it
   --> case.nvs:13:29
%A
error[E0462]: `$token` is `secret`, so `#[Db\Derive]` cannot convert it
%A
error[E0462]: `Core\Json::encode` cannot encode `Account`, because `Account::$apiKey` is `secret`
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
